#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:116 psr-4/PostTypeController.php:45
msgid "Search SiteGround accounts"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:117
msgid "Searches the SiteGround hosting accounts (one account per website/domain) that are imported into Orbis and returns their status, plan, server and expiration and billing dates. Accounts that are no longer present at SiteGround are excluded unless include_removed is true. Dates are in UTC. The _links of each account point to the Orbis page and to the hosting account in the SiteGround Client Area (my.siteground.com)."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:125
msgid "Search term, matched against the account name (domain name), the plan description, the server hostname, the server IP address and the data center."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:129
msgid "Limit the results to accounts with this SiteGround status."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:135
msgid "Limit the results to accounts with this SiteGround plan type, for example shared (StartUp), shared_plus (GrowBig), shared_geek (GoGeek) or cloud_lxc (Cloud)."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:139
msgid "Also return accounts that were not present in the latest SiteGround import."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:145
msgid "Only return accounts that expire before this date (YYYY-MM-DD)."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:150
msgid "Only return accounts that expire on or after this date (YYYY-MM-DD)."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:154
msgid "Maximum number of accounts to return."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:161 psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:264
msgid "Page of results to return."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:225 psr-4/PostTypeController.php:83
msgid "Search SiteGround websites"
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:226
msgid "Searches the SiteGround websites that are imported into Orbis and returns their domain, SiteGround account, status, CMS and server. One SiteGround account can host several websites. Websites that are no longer present at SiteGround are excluded unless include_removed is true. Dates are in UTC. SiteGround has two environments: the Client Area (my.siteground.com) for the SiteGround account, services, billing and websites, and Site Tools (tools.siteground.com) for managing a single website (files, databases, email, DNS, SSL, caching, backups and WordPress). The _links of each website point to the Orbis page, the website in the SiteGround Client Area, the Site Tools and the CMS admin."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:234
msgid "Search term, matched against the domain name, the account name, the server hostname, the server IP address and the data center."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:238
msgid "Limit the results to websites with this SiteGround status."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:244
msgid "Limit the results to websites with this CMS, for example wordpress, woocommerce or general."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:248
msgid "Limit the results to the websites of the SiteGround account with this SiteGround ID (siteground_id of the search-accounts ability)."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:252
msgid "Also return websites that were not present in the latest SiteGround import."
msgstr ""

#: psr-4/AbilitiesController.php:257
msgid "Maximum number of websites to return."
msgstr ""

